 limit. So Cand 5 is worse than Cand 2.\n\n**How much margin.** Real demand averages about 4.6% above the forecast. A plan that orders exactly the forecast (Cands 1 and 6) therefore drifts towards shortage. Each missing unit costs 24 for item 0 (lost price 16 plus penalty 8) and 23 for item 1.\n- A 10% margin cuts expected shortages by about 50 units of item 0 and about 29 of item 1. That gain is larger than the cost of buying roughly 110 + 50 extra units plus the extra holding.\n- A 20–25% margin (Cands 7 and 0) piles up stock: you pay for extra units, holding, and leftovers at the end. Cand 7 also overflows the warehouse on day 22, when 97 + 86 units arrive on top of what is already in stock.\n\n**Where Cand 2 loses.** On day 22, 168 units arrive on top of the leftover stock, so part of item 1 may overflow, costing about 100–200. That is not enough to drop it below Cands 6 and 3.\n\n**Expected order:** Cand 2 is best, then Cands 6 and 3 close behind, then Cands 7, 1 and 4, then Cands 5 and 0."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5015, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5015}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-25T18:58:29.175Z", "request_id": "req_011CgPTzGJYkMvhUTHM22tY8"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01RASt5pXrr6Y3n5gDoTTCei", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-